    "c2.examples": [
      {
        "title": "Connecting an article to an argument in a scientific essay",
        "typing": "\"How can I use this article to support my statement in my scientific essay?\"",
        "thinking": "I want to use this article in my scientific essay because I think it supports my statement, but I'm not sure how to make the connection. My statement is that schools should play a larger role in preventing child maltreatment. Based on its findings, I think that the article could support an argument about the importance of early identification and support in schools, but I am not sure how to translate this idea into a strong argument.",
        "processing": "The full text of the article is processed. Main findings, theoretical concepts, and conclusions are extracted. The most statistically likely \"helpful\" response pattern for \"how can I use this article to support my statement\" is activated. → Generate a comprehensive answer covering multiple possible ways to translate the article into an argument: relevant findings, connections between evidence and the statement, theoretical explanations, and possible ways to integrate the article into the essay. Present them as options. Sound confident and thorough.",
        "typing_note": "[upload a PDF]"
      },
      {
        "title": "Creating practice questions",
        "typing": "\"Make me some MCQs on chapter 4.\"",
        "thinking": "My exam is next week and I want to test myself on chapter 4. The professor always writes tricky MCQs where two options look almost the same and you have to know the exact definition to tell them apart. I need questions that are at that level, not the easy ones where you can guess by elimination.",
        "processing": "Full chapter text is processed. Key concepts, definitions, and relationships identified. \"MCQ\" triggers a default format: one correct answer, three distractors, medium difficulty, recall focused. → Generate questions that cover the chapter evenly, make distractors plausible but clearly distinguishable from the correct answer.",
        "typing_note": "[pastes chapter 4 text]"
      },
      {
        "title": "Summarizing a paper",
        "typing": "\"Can you summarize this paper?\"",
        "thinking": "I read this paper but I am not sure I understood the method section. I think they used a between subjects design but the way they describe the groups is confusing. I do not need a full summary, I just need someone to explain the design so I can figure out whether their conclusion actually follows from it.",
        "processing": "Full paper is processed. All sections weighted. \"Summarize\" triggers a default structure: background, aim, method, key findings, conclusion. Roughly equal coverage across sections. → Produce something that reads like a complete, balanced overview. Sound clear and organized.",
        "typing_note": "[uploads PDF]"
      },
      {
        "title": "Understanding a concept",
        "typing": "\"What are protective factors?\"",
        "thinking": "The professor used the term \"protective factors\" in the lecture today and I kind of got it from context, but when I tried to explain it to my friend I couldn't. I think it has something to do with factors that help children develop positively, but I am not sure how it differs from simply having a good environment or fewer risk factors.",
        "processing": "A definition request. \"Protective factors\" is a well represented concept in the training data. → Generate a clear, textbook style definition. Add an example. Possibly mention related terms. Present a self contained explanation, covering the concept broadly rather than targeting any specific point of confusion.",
        "typing_note": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Asking for feedback on your writing",
        "typing": "\"What do you think of this? Any feedback?\"",
        "thinking": "I spent two hours on this introduction and I think I explain the pedagogical dilemma clearly, but I am not sure whether the last two sentences lead naturally to my statement. My tutor told me last time that I tend to overcomplicate my sentences and explanations, and I want to know if I am doing that again here.",
        "processing": "A paragraph is provided. Feedback requested with no specific focus. → Scan for grammar, clarity, structure, and argument strength across the entire paragraph. Generate a balanced set of comments covering multiple aspects. Highlight positives first, then suggest improvements. Distribute attention evenly across the whole text.",
        "typing_note": "[pastes paragraph]"
      },
      {
        "title": "Writing a motivation letter",
        "typing": "\"Help me write a motivation letter for a youth care internship.\"",
